00:18:54.950 --> 00:19:19.299
Lorenzo Barisone: So here you have the website, where you can find more information about Swiss Ledger and the current project that has been developed and that are going on within the network. Essentially, from a technical point of view, governance and technical point of view, we have that Swiss Ledger is a public permission blockchain network where only authorized entities

126
00:19:19.300 --> 00:19:29.260
Lorenzo Barisone: can validate transactions by the permission that is… that today is granted by the City of Lugano, so the way in which

127
00:19:29.410 --> 00:19:53.900
Lorenzo Barisone: the city of Lugano make available to join the network is really, like, a public good, so it is a really open way, so you don't have to pay any kind of transaction cost to be there. The only cost that the persons that are within the network, the entities that are within the network, have to suffer.

128
00:19:53.900 --> 00:20:18.879
Lorenzo Barisone: is the infrastructure cost to maintain the node for the infrastructure. So, we use a proof-of-authority consensus mechanism, so providing fast, energy-efficient validation scheme with also a sandbox for regulatory compliance and policy-making development. From a technical point of view, it is built on Ethereum

129
00:20:18.880 --> 00:20:43.719
Lorenzo Barisone: virtual machine, and is anchored to Bitcoin and Ethereum to provide further public verifiability and network resilience. Today, we have more than 30 entities, which are on… both in the public and private sphere, but also in the academic context. So we have the University of Lugan.

130
00:20:43.720 --> 00:20:52.760
Lorenzo Barisone: and also the professional University of Lugano, which are part of the network. All the nodes are identical, in the sense that

131
00:20:52.790 --> 00:21:17.279
Lorenzo Barisone: All nodes are simple nodes, in the sense that they can act as relayers within the network, so resubmitting transaction, but then we have that some nodes has some additional capabilities, like the one of including transaction in blocks, and those are called validator nodes. So.

132
00:21:17.280 --> 00:21:33.459
Lorenzo Barisone: Adding a validator node requires the approval of the majority of the existence validator, and adding any node requires the approval, as I said before, of the Swiss Ledger Consortium that today is composed by the City of Lugano.

133
00:21:33.460 --> 00:21:56.709
Lorenzo Barisone: Probably in the future, we will move to a more consortium governance model in also entity terms, so that we will have a publicly funded association or foundation that will manage the project, always under the supervision and sponsorship of the City of Lugano.

134
00:21:56.750 --> 00:22:20.670
Lorenzo Barisone: It is a growing network, so in recent years, we had major companies and public entities that has decided to join the network, so we have the Canton Ticino, from what concerns the public entity context. Then we have some Swiss but global companies in terms of supply and

135
00:22:20.670 --> 00:22:45.670
Lorenzo Barisone: markets, like Avalok, which is the main provider for technological solutions within banks here in Switzerland. We have also Bitcoin Swiss, Signum Bank, HCL Tech Confinale Wealth Solutions, and recently we had also some tech companies, like Acer, that has decided to join the network, and Vargroup, which is

136
00:22:45.670 --> 00:22:55.219
Lorenzo Barisone: a company active in the IT, data science, and cybersecurity world, actively in Switzerland, Italy, and Spain.

137
00:22:55.490 --> 00:23:20.090
Lorenzo Barisone: So this is the list, the complete list. We are around 35 companies that are, part of the network. So from, as I said, from Acer, between Swiss, but also to some public entities, like the Canton Hospital of Ticino, the Canton Ticino, but also Tetr, Var Group, and the University of Lugana.

138
00:23:20.360 --> 00:23:44.319
Lorenzo Barisone: From a technical point of view, we have that the structure of Swiss Ledger is made of multiple layers, so we have a core ledger layer where transactions and assets are recorded, then we have a smart contract layer to, for the creation of smart contracts, API and integration layer to make possible to have applications

139
00:23:44.320 --> 00:24:08.629
Lorenzo Barisone: anchored to the blockchain for banks and fintech applications, a compliance layer made of an anti-money laundering AI detection system for fraudulent behavior, a security layer combining cryptographic and cybersecurity protection system, and an asset tokenization model, especially we have just recently

140
00:24:08.630 --> 00:24:22.960
Lorenzo Barisone: I mean, we are one of the blockchains under which can be used Adron, the tokenization platform of Tether, within the different kind of blockchains that are available within the tokenization tool.

141
00:24:23.370 --> 00:24:47.349
Lorenzo Barisone: So, we have different kind of applications that are already in place from some of the entities that are part of the network. For what concerns the private sector application, we are… we have the first tokenization certification platform through blockchain of a physical piece of art. This is a project called ArtChain.

142
00:24:47.350 --> 00:25:12.020
Lorenzo Barisone: and has been developed by, a company of Chinabit that is part of the, of the network, Active here in Switzerland. Essentially, this is the first blockchain-based certification system of physical piece of art that completely replaced, in terms of legal validity, the, physical certificates of piece of art.

143
00:25:12.020 --> 00:25:36.759
Lorenzo Barisone: And, for example, we have that the entire collection of Arnaldo Pomodoro, which is an Italian sculpture, is certified on the blockchain of the city of Lugano through Officina Beat and the Arnaldo Pomodoro Foundation. Then we have a company that is called Weekend Group, that is based in Geneva.

144
00:25:36.760 --> 00:26:01.609
Lorenzo Barisone: that provide KYB and KYC services, especially for financial institutions that uses Layer 2 Swiss Ledger to certify all the KYB and KYC processes through the blockchain of the city of Lugano Swiss Ledger. Then we have also other kind of notarization services for

