00:27:09.470 --> 00:27:34.330
Lorenzo Barisone: everything I will explain and that I have already described you. So, everything started in 2020 with the pandemic, so the worry, one of the worry of the municipality, of the government, of the city of Lugano, was that with the lockdown, people were getting used to buying online and reduce the civic engagement in

150
00:27:34.330 --> 00:27:42.269
Lorenzo Barisone: leaving the city and buying locally. So, what the city of Lugano has decided to,

151
00:27:42.420 --> 00:28:05.510
Lorenzo Barisone: I mean, to prevent this kind of worries at the time, was to create this city app that is my Lugano, and to create, within the city app, a sort of stablecoin. We cannot call it stablecoin, it is a payment token that is authorized by the Swiss Financial Authority.

152
00:28:05.510 --> 00:28:30.499
Lorenzo Barisone: and that is completely used, as I said, by more than 500 merchants within the city, so they accept the Luga as a means of payment. And the way in which, I mean, it's structured, we have that one Swiss franc is equal to 100 luga, so for what concern this aspect, it is

153
00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:55.429
